<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Upper Hesse</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Oberhessen</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> is a historical region of central Hesse in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giessen">Giessen</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vogelsberg">Vogelsberg</a> hills. From the early nineteenth century until 1937 it was one of the three provinces of the Grand Duchy and then the People's State of Hesse, with Giessen as its seat, separated from the southern provinces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/starkenburg">Starkenburg</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhenish-hesse">Rhenish Hesse</a> by territory around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a>.</p></div>
